[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605212150-etzhayyim-langserver-substrate", :adr/title "ADR-2605212150: etzhayyim-langserver — Fleet-resident LSP substrate on Murakumo Mac mini fleet", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605212150: etzhayyim-langserver — Fleet-resident LSP substrate on Murakumo Mac mini fleet\n\n**Status**: proposed\n**Date**: 2026-05-21\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nTwo converging pressures motivate a fleet-resident Language Server Protocol (LSP) substrate:\n\n1. **Editor side (human developers)**: a developer working on any Mac mini in the\n   Murakumo fleet (or on a roaming laptop joined to the mesh) should be able to\n   open an editor against the substrate code and receive symbol-aware\n   completion / hover / goto-definition / references / rename — without each\n   mini re-indexing the same rust/python/typescript workspace locally.\n\n2. **Cell side (Pregel)**: religious-corp Pregel cells (per ADR-2605192415) that\n   manipulate code — refactoring, dependency-walking, charter-compliance\n   verification — need a symbol-aware oracle. They currently lack one. A\n   fleet-resident LSP that any cell can query closes this gap.\n\nThe Murakumo fleet (10 tribes — naphtali / simeon / judah / zebulun / levi /\njoseph / issachar / dan / benjamin / asher; ADR-2605182312 + ADR-2605211910)\nis the sole Tier 1 compute target per ADR-2605191346, with launchd-only\ncontrol plane per ADR-2605192415 §7.1. A self-hosted mesh (`50-infra/cluster/\nmurakumo/`, X25519 + XChaCha20-Poly1305, 10.99.0.0/16 mesh subnet) provides\nfleet-wide L3 connectivity. The substrate to host LSPs and reach them\nfrom anywhere on the mesh therefore already exists; what is missing is the\n**glue** that turns \"a fleet\" into \"a federated LSP service\".\n\nReverse topological ordering of dependencies clarifies the build:\n\n```\nL1 host inventory      ←  L2 launchd plist   ← L3 LSP pins\n   ↓                        ↓                    ↓\nL4 socket / TCP listener ← L5 mesh-IP binding ← L6 health probe\n   ↓                        ↓                    ↓\nL7 observability         ← L8 editor bridge   ← L9 cell-runner integration\n```\n\nEach layer is independent of layers above it but closes a port for the layer\nbelow. Building leaf-first lets each commit ship with self-contained value\nand minimizes coupling.\n\n## Decision\n\nIntroduce `50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/` as a sibling of the existing\nreligious-corp infra modules (`etzhayyim-charters-compliance/`, `-tithe-router/`,\netc.). The module provides:\n\n### A. Architecture\n\n- **One LSP family per mini** (placement table below), chosen to avoid\n  co-locating heavy LSPs with the existing PDS (simeon), LiteLLM gateway\n  (judah), or heavy cron cells (levi).\n- **launchd-only supervision**, mirroring `com.etzhayyim.kotodama-cell-runner.plist`\n  conventions: `KeepAlive` on non-zero exit + network state, `ThrottleInterval`\n  15s anti-flap, `ProcessType` Background, `Nice` 5.\n- **socat fork mode** for transport: one LSP process spawned per client\n  connection. Cold-start cost paid by client; workspace cache persists\n  between sessions in the LSP's own cache directory.\n- **Both Unix domain socket + mesh-IP TCP listeners** by default (`mesh-both`\n  mode), so same-host editors get fast fs-permission auth and remote\n  editors traverse the mesh.\n\n### B. Placement\n\n| Language | LSP | Host | TCP port | Healthz port |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rust | rust-analyzer (`2026-01-13`) | joseph | 15510 | 15610 |\n| python | pyright (`1.1.401`) | issachar | 15511 | 15611 |\n| typescript | typescript-language-server (`4.3.4`) | dan | 15512 | 15612 |\n| go | gopls (`v0.18.1`) | naphtali | 15513 | 15613 |\n| lua | lua-language-server (`3.15.0`) | zebulun | 15514 | 15614 |\n| ruby | ruby-lsp (`0.23.0`) | naphtali | 15515 | 15615 |\n| _failover replica_ | (any) | asher | (dynamic) | (dynamic) |\n\nsolargraph is **explicitly not pinned** — superseded by Shopify ruby-lsp.\nPort range 15500-15600 LSP / 15600-15700 healthz; reserved space for ~84\nfuture languages.\n\n### C. Single source of truth\n\n`50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/scripts/lsp-fleet.json` (generated by\n`generate-fleet-registry.sh` from `hosts.toml` + `transports.toml` + `mesh.toml`)\nis the **only** place mesh-IPs and ports appear in editor-facing config.\nThe shim `scripts/attach-langserver.sh` reads it at editor-invocation time.\nEditor configs (nvim / Helix / Zed / VSCode) reference `attach-langserver.sh`\nand the language identifier; they never encode IPs. Fleet topology changes\nrequire only registry regen.\n\n### D. Observability\n\nThree signals to existing sinks; no new commercial vendor:\n\n1. on-disk via launchd `StandardOutPath` / `StandardErrorPath`, rotated by\n   macOS `newsyslog` (50 MiB × 5 archives, gzip);\n2. Prometheus textfile at `/metrics` on the healthz sidecar — five metrics\n   (`etzhayyim_langserver_up`, `_uptime_seconds`, `_probe_latency_seconds`\n   {probe=tcp|deep}, `_probe_failures_total`, `_probe_total`) scrape-target\n   `http://murakumo.etzhayyim.local:9090` (already in fleet.toml `[monitoring]`);\n3. NATS JetStream forwarder (`scripts/ship-logs-to-nats.sh`) — **opt-in\n   only**, default noop. Subject `etzhayyim.langserver.<host>.<lang>.<stream>`.\n\n### E. Cell-runner integration\n\n`40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/langserver_client.py`\nprovides an asyncio-based LSP JSON-RPC client (stdlib only, no third-party\ndeps), exposing `initialize / shutdown / hover / definition / references /\nrename`. The reference cell `LangserverHealthMonitoringCell` (registered\nin `50-infra/cluster/murakumo/cell-runner/cells.toml` on levi, cron\n`*/5 * * * *`, healthz 13028) concurrently probes every fleet LSP via real\nLSP `initialize` handshake and records latency + advertised capabilities.\n\n### F. Dry-run discipline (per CLAUDE.md)\n\nEvery generated artifact (plists, install scripts, NATS forwarder, attach\nshim) is **dry-run-default**. `launchctl load` is gated on:\n\n1. `scripts/probe-hardware.sh` committing `hw.*` blocks to `hosts.toml`\n2. `scripts/install-langservers.sh --apply` succeeding per host\n3. explicit user confirmation per CLAUDE.md \"ハードウェア未確認段階では\n   plist は dry-run のみ\" constraint.\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Cell symbol-awareness** unlocks substrate-internal refactor / verification\n  cells (e.g., a future `CharterRiderNoticeCell` that confirms a per-file\n  NOTICE update via gopls / pyright references rather than regex).\n- **Editor portability**: a developer can roam between minis (or attach\n  from a laptop) without dragging workspace indexes — the index lives on\n  the mini whose disk owns the source.\n- **No new commercial dependency**: socat / Prometheus / NATS / newsyslog\n  are Apache 2.0 (or BSD/MIT) OSS. Charter Rider applies to all\n  first-party artifacts in this module via repo-root `/CHARTER-RIDER.md`.\n- **Topology-change cost is one script run**: regenerate `lsp-fleet.json`,\n  no editor config edits.\n- **Health observability fits existing fleet conventions**: healthz\n  port allocation rule (`port_lsp + 100`) mirrors cell healthz at 13000-14000\n  + 100 offsets.\n\n### Negative\n\n- **socat fork mode pays cold-start per editor session**. rust-analyzer\n  indexing of large workspaces is the dominant cost. A future multiplexer\n  (`lsp-proxy` / `lsp-multiplexer`) can replace fork mode without changing\n  transports.toml — left to a follow-up ADR when the cost becomes\n  meaningful in practice.\n- **Workspace divergence**: the fleet LSP indexes the workspace on the\n  mini's disk, not the editor's local file tree. Developers editing\n  substrate code must `git pull` on the mini (or run an editor session\n  attached directly to the mini's workspace). Out-of-band workspace\n  synchronization is **out of scope** for this ADR.\n- **MST listener wiring deferred**: writing\n  `LangserverHealthMonitoringCell` results to MST requires a new lexicon\n  under `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/langserver/`. Captured in\n  `deps.toml [platform.langserver.cell_integration].lexicon_status =\n  \"deferred\"`; a follow-up ADR will register it.\n- **NATS deployment dependency for stream-tier observability**: NATS is\n  scaffolded (`50-infra/nats-jetstream-*`) but not yet live on every\n  mini. The forwarder is opt-in and gracefully no-ops if the broker is\n  unreachable.\n- **mesh identity legacy path**: `~/.etzhayyim/mesh/identity.json` lives on\n  current minis pending the cutover to `~/.etzhayyim/mesh/identity.json`.\n  `langserver_client` reads either path; this is a temporary compatibility\n  shim that disappears when the cutover lands.\n\n### Constitutional & substrate-fit checks\n\n- **State**: LSP is **computation only**. No MST / IPFS / L2 writes from\n  this substrate. Passes ADR-2605172000 kotoba check.\n- **Payment**: none. Passes ADR-2605172100.\n- **License**: Apache 2.0 + Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 (per ADR-2605192200).\n- **Operating entity**: all artifacts use `etzhayyim-` prefix. No `etzhayyim-`\n  prefix in newly authored code. Per CLAUDE.md.\n- **Eros / Gore / Force**: not applicable — developer tooling has no\n  generative content surface.\n- **Land trust**: not applicable.\n- **Religious-corp daemon architecture (ADR-2605192415 §7.1)**: this\n  substrate **adds** a peer to the existing launchd daemon family. It is\n  not a religious-corp constitutional cell — placement on `levi` for the\n  reference monitoring cell is a *workload* decision, not a constitutional\n  binding.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### A. One LSP container image per language, pulled by every mini\n\nRejected. Container orchestration is forbidden per ADR-2605191346 (no\ncommercial K8s control plane). Standalone container runtimes (orbstack /\nlima) exist but launchd already supervises the existing kotodama\ncell-runner — adding a parallel control plane buys nothing.\n\n### B. Run all LSPs on a single \"tool box\" mini\n\nRejected. The fleet's Wellbecoming axis (per ADR-2605192100 §1.13)\napplies to infrastructure too: concentration risk on a single mini is a\nflap-cascade risk. Distribution across 5 tribes (joseph / issachar / dan /\nnaphtali / zebulun) with `asher` as failover replica matches the\nfleet's existing scheduling discipline.\n\n### C. Editor-side LSP only (no fleet daemon)\n\nRejected for the Pregel-cell use case: cells can't drive an editor.\nRejected for the developer use case at fleet-scale: re-indexing rust\nworkspaces on every editor restart, per developer, per mini, multiplies\nthe indexing cost by N × M where the federated approach is O(1).\n\n### D. Adopt commercial managed solution (e.g., Coder / Gitpod)\n\nRejected. ADR-2605191346 hard rule against commercial K8s control plane\n+ Charter Rider §2(a)-(h) commercial-dependency category. OSS only.\n\n### E. Use Tailscale instead of self-hosted mesh\n\nRejected. The fleet already runs `murakumo-mesh` (50-infra/cluster/\nmurakumo/, X25519 + XChaCha20-Poly1305). Reusing it avoids a second\nidentity/key system and a SaaS dependency (Tailscale control plane).\n\n### F. Build a custom WebSocket LSP gateway\n\nConsidered for browser-based editor support. Rejected at this stage —\nadds a JS runtime to the substrate; existing 4 desktop editors (nvim /\nHelix / Zed / VSCode) cover the developer surface. Re-evaluate if a\nbrowser editor (e.g., Theia, code-server) is requested.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2604251830 (Shannon-Optimal 8-Layer Architecture)\n- ADR-2605170900 (etzhayyim/root as canonical home for religious-corp open ADRs)\n- ADR-2605182312 (Local Bring-up of Artificial Organism on Murakumo Fleet)\n- ADR-2605191346 (Murakumo Mac-mini fleet as sole Tier 1 deployment target)\n- ADR-2605192415 (Religious-Corp Pregel Daemon Architecture — Tier 1 launchd 常駐)\n- ADR-2605192200 (Apache 2.0 + Charter Compliance Rider v2.0)\n- ADR-2605211910 (Murakumo Fleet LAN IP Rebaseline — Ethernet-side IPs)\n- `50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/` — module root\n- `50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/README.edn` — 9-layer status table\n- `50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/{hosts,transports,mesh,obs}.toml` — per-layer SSoTs\n- `50-infra/etzhayyim-langserver/scripts/lsp-fleet.json` — generated registry\n- `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/primitives/langserver_{client,murakumo}.py` — cell-side library + ref cell\n- `50-infra/cluster/murakumo/cell-runner/cells.toml` — `LangserverHealthMonitoringCell` entry\n- `deps.toml` `[platform.langserver.*]` — six sub-tables mirroring per-layer SSoTs\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605212150-etzhayyim-langserver-substrate.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "etzhayyim-langserver", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-21", :adr/date "2026-05-21", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["2605191346-etzhayyim-vultr-free-murakumo-control-plane  # Murakumo Mac-mini fleet as sole Tier 1 deployment target" "adr-2605171800-langgraph-mst-ipfs-l2-anchor-pipeline  # LangGraph Pregel ← MST ← IPFS ← L2 pipeline"], :adr/authoritative_for ["etzhayyim-langserver substrate design" "LSP daemon placement on Murakumo fleet" "cell-runner ↔ LSP query path"]}]
